\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Spatial dose--response} (depth probe for the residual niche gap). Per-cell representations are progressively spatial-smoothed over $k$ nearest spatial neighbours ($x$, log scale; $k{=}0$ is per-cell); $y$ is supervised niche prediction under spatially-blocked CV---\textbf  {(A)} $k$NN macro-AUROC and \textbf  {(B)} macro-F1. Smoothing per-cell PCA (blue) lifts niche prediction monotonically (F1 Spearman $\rho =0.98$) from the per-cell-FM level past all three raw spatial FMs and the composition baseline (dotted references) by $k\approx 25$--$50$; the same dose helps a smoothed FM (orange) too. The residual ``spatial-FM gap'' is therefore the spatial-aggregation axis---one operation a per-cell model lacks---not a representational deficit.}}{12}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spatialdose}{{5}{12}{\emph {Spatial dose--response} (depth probe for the residual niche gap). Per-cell representations are progressively spatial-smoothed over $k$ nearest spatial neighbours ($x$, log scale; $k{=}0$ is per-cell); $y$ is supervised niche prediction under spatially-blocked CV---\textbf {(A)} $k$NN macro-AUROC and \textbf {(B)} macro-F1. Smoothing per-cell PCA (blue) lifts niche prediction monotonically (F1 Spearman $\rho =0.98$) from the per-cell-FM level past all three raw spatial FMs and the composition baseline (dotted references) by $k\approx 25$--$50$; the same dose helps a smoothed FM (orange) too. The residual ``spatial-FM gap'' is therefore the spatial-aggregation axis---one operation a per-cell model lacks---not a representational deficit}{figure.caption.22}{}}
